invariant: INV-26
file: quic_gcm.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: quic_gcm.c guards its AES=hw arm on a macro no build defines, so
  an AES=hw object runs the portable 128-step multiply under the AES=hw
  name. Nothing else objects. quic_ghash_hw.c still compiles and links
  and defines two functions nobody calls, and bin/ghash_equiv_test, the
  published vectors and the Wycheproof suite all pass, because the
  portable GHASH computes the same bytes; only the time is wrong, by the
  factor docs/quic.md measures. The design refuses a silent fall back:
  AES=hw is a statement about what the object contains. The script
  compiles quic_gcm.c with -DCH_AES_HW and requires its object to call
  both entries quic_ghash_hw.c defines.

--- old
#ifdef CH_AES_HW
// AES=hw: quic_ghash_hw.c computes both GHASH steps on the carry-less
--- new
#ifdef CH_GHASH_HW
// AES=hw: quic_ghash_hw.c computes both GHASH steps on the carry-less
